  "question": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> gas is liquefied at <math><msup><mrow><mn>27</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> . Gas follows the following graph during liquefaction for 1 mole of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> .<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/635177_1.JPG\" style=\"width: 276px; height: 216px;\" /><br />\rThen which statement is (are) correct in gaseous phase will<br />\r(i) The maximum density of gas is 0.1 gm/ml<br />\r(ii) The density of liquid <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is 1 g/ml at 60 atm.<br />\r(iii) At point C 50% of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is liquefied.<br />\r(iv) The compressibility factor of gas at <math><msup><mrow><mn>27</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is always less than 1.<br />\rWhich of the above is/are correct",
